# Hashed build assets must fail as real 404s. Without this rule they fall through to the
# SPA catch-all below and the server answers a .js request with index.html, which the
# browser rejects: "Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module script but the server responded
# with a MIME type of text/html". Anyone still holding an index.html from a previous
# deploy then gets a blank page instead of a recoverable error.
/assets/*  /404.html  404

# Everything else is client-side routing and must serve the app shell.
/*  /index.html  200
